/*! \page sdk_class_b Class-B Scheduler Authoring

Markdown companions:
- Packaging / deadline / accelerators: \c docs/class_b_accelerator_authoring.md
- Baseline pipeline (MCS / pack / TPC): \c docs/class_b_scheduler_baseline.md

\section sdk_b_boundary Boundary

Synchronous in-process host records; ~100 us complete boundary; conventional
result retained on error or evaluation mode. No inherited PUSCH stream.

\section sdk_b_baseline Baseline reference pipeline

\c ref_scheduler_cpu runs \c run_scheduler_pipeline: rank, package OLLA,
table-aware MCS, multi-UE free-VRB packing, UL TPC. Intent bits are gated by
host \c allowed_output_flags (\c emit_only_allowed). Host YAML
\c scheduler_allow_* must be accepted by the native invoke path
(\c ALLOW_KNOWN_MASK). See the baseline Markdown guide for algorithms and the
source map under \c reference/common/reference_scheduler_pipeline.cpp.

\section sdk_b_accel Internal accelerators

Declaring \c cuda admits an accelerator backend for reporting. The module owns
transfers and synchronization and must return host intent before the deadline.
No resident Class-B tensor ABI in v1. Reference remains \c ref_scheduler_cpu.

\section sdk_b_eval Evaluation mode

DU \c scheduler_evaluation_only measures the dApp while discarding valid
decisions. Not lifecycle SHADOW.

\section sdk_b_run Enable on a DU

Reference \c ref_scheduler_cpu (UUID \c …000006): stage package, YAML with
evaluation then \c scheduler_allow_* + \c scheduler_evaluation_only:false,
E3 load in-process/cpu → prepare → arm → shadow → activate.
Full cookbook: Markdown \c docs/run_examples.md §3 and
\c docs/class_b_accelerator_authoring.md (enable section).

*/
